---
import BaseLayout from "../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much Do GLP-1 Drugs Cost? A Plain Guide (2026) | GLP Index"
  description="List price, GoodRx, manufacturer savings cards, insurance, and telehealth. Here is what Wegovy, Mounjaro, Zepbound, and Ozempic actually cost under each pricing path in 2026."
  ogImage="/og-glp1-cost-guide.png"
>
  <Header />

  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumbs">
        <a href="/">GLP Index</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/guides/">Guides</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="now">GLP-1 cost guide</span>
      </div>
      <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 20px">Pricing · Updated May 2026</div>
      <h1 class="serif" style="font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(34px,4.5vw,56px);max-width:22ch">
        How much do GLP-1 drugs <em>actually</em> cost?
      </h1>
      <p class="deck" style="margin-top:18px;max-width:58ch">
        List price is over $1,000 a month for most of these drugs. What you pay is almost always different. Here is a plain breakdown of every pricing path.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="guide-layout">

      <aside class="toc">
        <h4>On this page</h4>
        <a href="#overview">Pricing overview</a>
        <a href="#list-price">List price</a>
        <a href="#goodrx">GoodRx</a>
        <a href="#savings-cards">Savings cards</a>
        <a href="#insurance">Insurance</a>
        <a href="#telehealth">Telehealth</a>
        <a href="#compounded">Compounded</a>
        <a href="#calculator">Use the calculator</a>
      </aside>

      <article class="prose guide-body">

        <div class="price-intro" id="overview">
          <p>
            There is no single answer to what a GLP-1 drug costs, because the same prescription can cost anywhere from $0 to $1,400 per month depending on your insurance, which pharmacy you use, whether you qualify for a savings program, and whether you go through a traditional pharmacy or a telehealth provider.
          </p>
          <p>
            The sections below cover each path. The cost comparison calculator on this site shows current estimates side by side.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 id="list-price">List price (without anything else)</h2>
        <p>
          List price is what the drug costs at a pharmacy with no insurance, no discount card, no savings program. Almost nobody pays this number, but it sets the ceiling.
        </p>

        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Drug</th>
              <th>Active ingredient</th>
              <th>Approved for</th>
              <th>Est. list price / month</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Wegovy</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 2.4mg</td>
              <td class="muted">Obesity</td>
              <td class="num">~$1,350</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Wegovy HD</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 7.2mg</td>
              <td class="muted">Obesity</td>
              <td class="num">~$1,500</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Zepbound</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">tirzepatide</td>
              <td class="muted">Obesity</td>
              <td class="num">~$1,060</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Mounjaro</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">tirzepatide</td>
              <td class="muted">Type 2 diabetes</td>
              <td class="num">~$1,070</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Ozempic</strong></td>
              <td class="muted">semaglutide 1mg</td>
              <td class="muted">Type 2 diabetes</td>
              <td class="num">~$950</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="table-note">
          Prices are estimates based on GoodRx data and pharmacy list prices as of May 2026. Actual prices vary by pharmacy and location. Use the <a href="/cost-comparison/">cost comparison calculator</a> for current estimates.
        </p>

        <h2 id="goodrx">GoodRx and discount cards</h2>
        <p>
          GoodRx negotiates discounted rates with pharmacies through pharmacy benefit managers. You do not need insurance to use it. You use a GoodRx coupon at checkout instead of insurance.
        </p>
        <p>
          For GLP-1 drugs, GoodRx savings vary but are typically 10 to 30% below list price at certain pharmacies. The bigger savings come from the manufacturer programs below. GoodRx is most useful if you do not qualify for a manufacturer savings card or need coverage at a specific pharmacy.
        </p>
        <p>
          You cannot stack GoodRx with insurance. You use one or the other per transaction.
        </p>

        <h2 id="savings-cards">Manufacturer savings cards</h2>
        <p>
          Both Novo Nordisk (Wegovy) and Eli Lilly (Zepbound, Mounjaro) run savings programs directly. These can meaningfully lower what you pay.
        </p>

        <div class="savings-cards">
          <div class="savings-card">
            <div class="sc-maker">Novo Nordisk</div>
            <div class="sc-drugs mono">Wegovy · Wegovy HD</div>
            <div class="sc-program">NovoCare Savings Program</div>
            <div class="sc-details">
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">With commercial insurance</span>
                <span class="sc-val">As low as $0/month (varies by plan)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">Without insurance</span>
                <span class="sc-val">Eligibility-based discount program</span>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">Not eligible</span>
                <span class="sc-val">Medicare, Medicaid, federal programs</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="savings-card">
            <div class="sc-maker">Eli Lilly</div>
            <div class="sc-drugs mono">Zepbound · Mounjaro</div>
            <div class="sc-program">LillyDirect Savings Program</div>
            <div class="sc-details">
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">With commercial insurance</span>
                <span class="sc-val">As low as $25/month</span>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">Self-pay (no insurance)</span>
                <span class="sc-val">~$549/month (Zepbound vials)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row">
                <span class="sc-key">Not eligible</span>
                <span class="sc-val">Medicare, Medicaid, federal programs</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p>
          Savings cards are not available to people on Medicare, Medicaid, or other federal insurance programs. This is a federal anti-kickback rule, not a company decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lilly's $549/month self-pay option (Zepbound vials through LillyDirect) is one of the most accessible cash-pay paths available for a branded GLP-1 as of 2026. It requires no insurance and ships directly.
        </p>

        <h2 id="insurance">Insurance</h2>
        <p>
          Insurance coverage for GLP-1 drugs for obesity is inconsistent and changing. Coverage for the diabetes-approved versions (Ozempic, Mounjaro) is more common than for the obesity-approved versions (Wegovy, Zepbound).
        </p>

        <div class="factor-list">
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Employer-sponsored plans</div>
            <p>Coverage varies widely. Some plans cover Wegovy or Zepbound for obesity, others do not. Call the number on your insurance card and ask specifically whether your plan covers GLP-1 medications for weight management, and what the copay is under your specific formulary.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Medicare</div>
            <p>Medicare Part D does not cover GLP-1 drugs for obesity alone. Coverage may apply if you have a qualifying diagnosis like type 2 diabetes or cardiovascular disease. The landscape here is evolving, so confirm current coverage with Medicare directly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Medicaid</div>
            <p>Medicaid coverage varies by state. Some states cover GLP-1 drugs; others do not. Contact your state Medicaid office or your prescriber's office, which typically handles prior authorization.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="factor">
            <div class="factor-label">Prior authorization</div>
            <p>Most insurance plans that do cover these drugs require prior authorization. Your doctor submits documentation showing you meet the criteria (typically BMI above a certain threshold, sometimes plus a comorbidity). This adds time but is a standard part of the coverage process.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="telehealth">Telehealth providers</h2>
        <p>
          Telehealth platforms can prescribe GLP-1 medications online, often with faster access than a traditional doctor's office. Most offer a bundled price that includes the consultation and medication.
        </p>
        <p>
          Pricing through telehealth is often comparable to or slightly above what you would pay with a manufacturer savings card at a traditional pharmacy, but includes the convenience of an online visit and home delivery.
        </p>
        <p>
          What to verify before signing up with a telehealth provider:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Whether they prescribe brand-name medications or compounded versions (see below)</li>
          <li>Whether they accept your insurance</li>
          <li>What the monthly subscription includes versus what is extra</li>
          <li>Whether you can pause or cancel without penalty</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="compounded">Compounded semaglutide and tirzepatide</h2>

        <div class="callout-warn-box">
          <p class="callout-head">FDA shortage status changed in early 2025.</p>
          <p>Semaglutide was removed from the FDA drug shortage list in February 2025. Tirzepatide followed shortly after. Large-scale compounding of these drugs by 503B outsourcing facilities is no longer permitted now that the shortage designation has ended. Some 503A pharmacies can still compound for individual patient-specific reasons, but broad commercial availability has narrowed significantly.</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          Compounded semaglutide was widely available from telehealth providers in 2023 and 2024, often at significantly lower prices than brand-name Wegovy. The FDA shortage designation that allowed this ended in early 2025.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a provider is currently offering compounded semaglutide or tirzepatide at scale, verify their regulatory compliance carefully. FDA-approved brand-name medications (Wegovy, Zepbound, Mounjaro, Ozempic) are the versions with the clinical trial data behind them.
        </p>

        <div class="cta-box" id="calculator">
          <div class="cta-inner">
            <div>
              <p class="cta-title serif">See current prices side by side</p>
              <p class="cta-sub">The cost comparison calculator shows GoodRx, savings card, and telehealth pricing for each drug, updated monthly.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="btn btn-p" href="/cost-comparison/">
              Open calculator <span class="arr">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="source-footer">
          <p class="source-label mono">Sources</p>
          <p>Drug pricing: GoodRx and pharmacy list prices as of May 2026. Manufacturer savings program details: NovoCare and LillyDirect program terms as of May 2026. FDA shortage status: <a href="https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/drugshortages/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FDA Drug Shortages database ↗</a></p>
        </div>

      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: 56px 0 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .guide-layout {
    padding: 64px 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: 88px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .toc h4 {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .toc a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 0 6px 14px;
    color: #3A352E;
    border-left: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
    margin-left: -15px;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .toc a:hover { color: #3F5D52; border-left-color: #3F5D52; }

  .guide-body { max-width: 680px; min-width: 0; }

  .price-intro p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  /* Tables */
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 24px 0 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .data-table thead th {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .data-table tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE7DC; }
  .data-table tbody tr:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .data-table tbody td { padding: 12px 12px; color: #3A352E; }

  .data-table td.num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1A1815;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .data-table td.muted { color: #6B655C; font-size: 13px; }

  .table-note {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .table-note a { color: #3F5D52; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 30%, transparent); }

  /* Savings cards */
  .savings-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
  }

  .savings-card {
    background: #FBFAF7;
    border: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
  }

  .sc-maker {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1A1815;
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .sc-drugs {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #3F5D52;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .sc-program {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE7DC;
  }

  .sc-details { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }

  .sc-row { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }

  .sc-key {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #6B655C;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .sc-val {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #1A1815;
  }

  /* Factor list */
  .factor-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
  }

  .factor {
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #EDE7DC;
  }

  .factor:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .factor-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #3F5D52;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .factor p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* Warning callout */
  .callout-warn-box {
    background: #FFF7E8;
    border: 1px solid #E8C97A;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 24px 0 20px;
  }

  .callout-head {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1A1815;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .callout-warn-box p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-box {
    background: #1A1815;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    margin: 48px 0 40px;
  }

  .cta-inner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .cta-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #FBFAF7;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .cta-sub {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #9D968C;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .cta-box a.btn-p {
    color: #FBFAF7;
    border-bottom: none;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .cta-box a.btn-p:hover { color: #FBFAF7; }

  /* Source */
  .source-footer {
    padding-top: 32px;
    border-top: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .source-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .source-footer p {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #6B655C;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .source-footer a {
    color: #3F5D52;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 30%, transparent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .guide-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .toc { position: static; }
    .cta-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .guide-layout { padding: 40px 0; }
    .savings-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .data-table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; font-size: 13px; }
    .data-table thead th, .data-table tbody td { padding: 10px 8px; }
    .cta-box { padding: 20px 16px; }
    .cta-inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
    .callout-warn-box { padding: 16px 18px; }
    .page-head { padding: 32px 0 24px; }
  }
</style>
